#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:1
msgid "Catalog-Generated Intrinsics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:3
msgid ""
"Most cuda-oxide device intrinsics are not implemented by editing compiler "
"stages independently. They are described as reviewed catalog inputs and "
"`cuda-intrinsics-gen` generates the repetitive API, dialect, importer, "
"lowering, target, reference, and probe surfaces from that contract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:8
msgid ""
"Use this workflow when the intrinsic fits the generated catalog model. For "
"an operation that requires bespoke verification or lowering that the catalog "
"cannot express, use [Adding New Intrinsics](adding-new-intrinsics.md) "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:14
msgid "Choose the Right Path First"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:16
msgid ""
"Before editing anything, find the nearest existing intrinsic with the same "
"semantic and lowering shape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:19
msgid ""
"Does an existing catalog family model the intrinsic?\n"
"    |\n"
"    +-- yes -> extend that overlay family and the ABI ledger\n"
"    |\n"
"    +-- no  -> determine whether the generator needs a new family/shape\n"
"               or whether the operation is genuinely hand-written\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:28
msgid ""
"An LLVM declaration by itself is not enough to admit an intrinsic. The "
"catalog also records cuda-oxide policy such as its Rust API, safety and "
"effects, expected PTX form, target requirements, ABI identity, and lowering "
"evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:32
msgid ""
"The normal contribution path is therefore to extend an existing reviewed "
"family, not to edit generated Rust files or `intrinsics/catalog.json` "
"directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:37
msgid "Sources of Truth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:39
msgid ""
"The generated intrinsic pipeline is assembled from reviewed inputs and "
"resolved into a generated catalog:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:42
msgid ""
"intrinsics/upstream.lock -> intrinsics/imported.json ----\\\n"
"intrinsics/overlay.toml -> intrinsics/overlay/*.toml -----+\n"
"intrinsics/abi-v1.toml -----------------------------------+--> resolve\n"
"intrinsics/evidence/*.json -------------------------------/       |\n"
"                                                                  v\n"
"                                                     intrinsics/catalog."
"json\n"
"                                                            GENERATED\n"
"                                                                  |\n"
"                                                                  v\n"
"                                                        generated outputs\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:55
msgid "Their roles are different:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "File / artifact"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "Role"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "`intrinsics/upstream.lock`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "Pins the LLVM source/extraction identity used by the imported facts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "`intrinsics/imported.json`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid ""
"Records what the pinned LLVM/NVPTX source declares. Normal intrinsic "
"additions consume this committed file; they do not rerun extraction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "`intrinsics/overlay.toml`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "Explicitly indexes the admitted overlay shards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "`intrinsics/overlay/*.toml`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "Records cuda-oxide policy for reviewed intrinsic families."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "`intrinsics/abi-v1.toml`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "Append-only stable intrinsic ABI ledger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "`intrinsics/evidence/*.json`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "Records reviewed lowering evidence when the route requires it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "`intrinsics/catalog.json`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:0
msgid "Resolved generated plan. Do not edit it by hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:67
msgid ""
"Generated sources and probe/reference outputs carry a `DO NOT EDIT` marker. "
"Change their source inputs and regenerate instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:70
msgid "Catalog Metadata"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:72
msgid ""
"The overlay manifest carries version and backend metadata for the resolved "
"catalog. These values describe the catalog contract; they are not per-"
"intrinsic knobs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:76
msgid ""
"There are two distinct `schema` numbers in play, one per side of the "
"generator:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:79
msgid ""
"intrinsics/overlay.toml   schema = 44   (overlay input format)\n"
"        | cuda-intrinsics-gen\n"
"        v\n"
"intrinsics/catalog.json   \"schema\": 46  (serialized catalog format)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:86
msgid ""
"`schema` (in `overlay.toml`) identifies the overlay **input** format the "
"generator accepts (`OVERLAY_SCHEMA` in `crates/cuda-intrinsics-gen/src/"
"resolve/overlay.rs`); the resolver rejects a mismatched manifest. It is not "
"the catalog format version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:90
msgid "`catalog_version` identifies the reviewed catalog contract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:91
msgid ""
"`intrinsic_abi` identifies the intrinsic ABI generation whose stable entries "
"are recorded in `intrinsics/abi-v1.toml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:93
msgid ""
"`backend_profile` selects the reviewed backend profile used while resolving "
"lowering evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:96
msgid ""
"Contributors normally change these values only as part of a deliberate "
"catalog, ABI, or backend-profile transition. Do not synthesize or edit "
"corresponding metadata directly in generated `intrinsics/catalog.json`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:100
msgid "catalog.json Header Fields"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:102
msgid ""
"The generated catalog stamps its own header at resolve time. For reference, "
"since the file is generated and otherwise undocumented:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:105
msgid ""
"`schema`: version of the **serialized catalog** format (`CATALOG_SCHEMA` in "
"the same `resolve/overlay.rs`). Distinct from the overlay's `schema`; see "
"the sketch above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:108
msgid ""
"`catalog_version`: the reviewed catalog contract, copied from `overlay.toml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:110
msgid ""
"`intrinsic_abi`: the ABI generation, copied from `overlay.toml`; its stable "
"entries live in `intrinsics/abi-v1.toml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:112
msgid ""
"`generator_version`: the `cuda-intrinsics-gen` crate version that produced "
"the catalog (its Cargo package version). The same value appears in the "
"`@generated by cuda-intrinsics-gen <version>` banner of every generated file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:119
msgid "The Normal Workflow: Extend an Existing Family"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:121
msgid "1. Find the nearest sibling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:123
msgid ""
"Start in `intrinsics/overlay/`, not in generated Rust code and not by "
"scrolling `intrinsics/imported.json`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:126
msgid ""
"Find an existing entry with the same family and lowering shape, then use the "
"imported LLVM facts only for the fields that must agree with upstream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:129
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:131
msgid ""
"grep -R 'id = \"<nearest-sibling>\"' intrinsics/overlay\n"
"rg '<llvm-or-record-name>' intrinsics/imported.json\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:136
msgid ""
"Prefer copying a proven sibling over constructing an entry from scratch. The "
"resolver is intentionally fail-closed, but matching the established family "
"shape keeps the review small and makes unexpected generated diffs easier to "
"spot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:141
msgid "2. Add or extend the overlay entry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:143
msgid "Edit the appropriate file under:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:145
msgid "intrinsics/overlay/<family>.toml\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:149
msgid ""
"The overlay is the hand-edited policy input. Do not edit the corresponding "
"operation under `crates/dialect-nvvm/src/ops/generated/`, the generated "
"importer dispatch, generated lowering tables, or `intrinsics/catalog.json`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:153
msgid ""
"If the contribution requires a **new overlay shard**, also add that shard to "
"the sorted `shards` list in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:156
msgid "intrinsics/overlay.toml\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:160
msgid ""
"`generate` and `check` reconcile the index with the overlay directory and "
"reject an unindexed shard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:163
msgid "3. Append the ABI ledger entry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:165
msgid "Add the new stable identity at the end of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:167
msgid "intrinsics/abi-v1.toml\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:171
msgid ""
"The ledger is append-only. Existing entries must not be reordered, deleted, "
"renumbered, or repurposed. The catalog identity, operation key, and raw Rust "
"signature must agree with the overlay entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:175
msgid ""
"Treat the ABI ID as a merge-time resource. If another intrinsic PR lands "
"first, rebase onto the latest `main`, append after the new ledger tail, and "
"regenerate. Do not preserve an obsolete numeric range merely because the "
"branch used it earlier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:180
msgid "4. Handle lowering evidence only when needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:182
msgid ""
"If the new intrinsic uses an already-reviewed lowering/evidence shape, "
"follow the existing sibling contract. A normal catalog addition does not "
"necessarily need a new evidence file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:186
msgid ""
"If the backend route is new and needs candidate evidence, use an explicit "
"candidate probe:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:189
msgid ""
"HOST=\"$(rustc -vV | sed -n 's/^host: //p')\"\n"
"LLC=\"$(rustc --print sysroot)/lib/rustlib/$HOST/bin/llc\"\n"
"\n"
"cargo run -p cuda-intrinsics-gen -- probe --candidate \\\n"
"  --intrinsic <catalog-id> \\\n"
"  --llc \"$LLC\" \\\n"
"  --gpu-target <sm-target> \\\n"
"  --ptx-feature <ptx-feature> \\\n"
"  --ptxas <path-to-ptxas>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:201
msgid ""
"On a system where terminal assembly is deliberately unavailable, replace `--"
"ptxas <path-to-ptxas>` with the explicit `--skip-terminal` flag. Candidate "
"mode requires one of those choices; it does not silently fall back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:205
msgid ""
"Review candidate output before promoting any evidence into the committed "
"contract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:208
msgid "5. Regenerate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:210
msgid "Run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:212
msgid "cargo run -p cuda-intrinsics-gen -- generate\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:216
msgid "Then inspect the working tree and diff before running broader checks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:218
msgid ""
"git status --short\n"
"git diff --stat\n"
"git diff -- intrinsics crates/cuda-intrinsics crates/cuda-device \\\n"
"  crates/dialect-nvvm crates/mir-importer crates/mir-lower \\\n"
"  crates/cuda-oxide-codegen crates/rustc-codegen-cuda\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:226
msgid ""
"Check `git status --short` as well: newly created overlay or evidence files "
"are untracked until staged and therefore do not appear in `git diff`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:229
msgid ""
"For an addition that fits an existing family, generated changes should "
"follow the sibling pattern. Unexpected unrelated changes are a reason to "
"stop and recheck the overlay, ledger, evidence, or branch base."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:235
msgid "Validate Before Pushing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:237
msgid ""
"The repository provides one local entry point for the generated-intrinsics "
"CI contract:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:240
msgid "just check-intrinsics upstream/main\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:244
msgid "Use the actual PR base if it is not `upstream/main`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:246
msgid ""
"That recipe mirrors the generated-intrinsics CI job and currently covers the "
"three load-bearing checks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:249
msgid ""
"cuda-intrinsics-gen check\n"
"cuda-intrinsics-gen probe --all --skip-terminal --per-target\n"
"cuda-intrinsics-gen check-abi-history --base-ref <base>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:255
msgid ""
"Use `just check-intrinsics ...` as the normal contributor interface rather "
"than copying the underlying commands into scripts. The recipe can evolve "
"when the CI contract gains additional coverage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:259
msgid "Two environment requirements the gates carry with them:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:261
msgid ""
"`check-abi-history` walks git history back to the base ref, so it needs a "
"full clone. CI checks out with `fetch-depth: 0`; a shallow local clone can "
"fail to resolve the base."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:264
msgid ""
"The generator shells out to `rustfmt` when it writes generated sources. That "
"is why `rust-toolchain.toml` pins the `rustfmt` component; no extra install "
"is needed on a normal checkout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:268
msgid "For a focused probe while developing one intrinsic, you can also run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:270
msgid ""
"cargo run -p cuda-intrinsics-gen -- probe \\\n"
"  --intrinsic <catalog-id> \\\n"
"  --skip-terminal\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:276
msgid ""
"Finally, run the normal checks required by the files you changed. For "
"changes that also update the book:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:279
msgid ""
"just book\n"
"bash scripts/check-book-api-names.sh\n"
"git diff --check\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:287
msgid "When the Existing Catalog Cannot Express It"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:289
msgid ""
"A missing sibling is a design signal. If the intrinsic requires a lowering "
"shape, operand adapter, result contract, or family structure the generator "
"does not model, the change is no longer a small catalog admission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:293
msgid "A new generated shape typically involves generator code such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:295
msgid ""
"crates/cuda-intrinsics-gen/src/model/\n"
"crates/cuda-intrinsics-gen/src/resolve/\n"
"crates/cuda-intrinsics-gen/src/render/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:301
msgid ""
"and may also require real compiler lowering changes under `crates/mir-lower/"
"` or `crates/dialect-nvvm/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:304
msgid ""
"Keep that work separate from routine catalog admission when possible. The "
"ABI ledger and generated-intrinsics validation contract still apply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:307
msgid ""
"If the operation instead needs bespoke verification or lowering by design "
"and should remain outside the catalog, follow the hand-written workflow in "
"[Adding New Intrinsics](adding-new-intrinsics.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:313
msgid "Extraction Is Not Part of a Normal Addition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:315
msgid ""
"The `extract` command refreshes imported LLVM facts. It is for an LLVM "
"source or pin update, not for adding an intrinsic that already exists in the "
"committed `intrinsics/imported.json`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:319
msgid ""
"Normal additions consume the committed imported facts. This keeps routine "
"intrinsic work independent of an LLVM checkout and makes the reviewed "
"overlay, ABI ledger, and evidence the explicit cuda-oxide policy layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:325
msgid "What Not to Edit by Hand"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:327
msgid "For a catalog-generated intrinsic, do not directly edit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:329
msgid "`intrinsics/catalog.json`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:330
msgid "generated files under `crates/cuda-intrinsics/src/generated/`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:331
msgid "generated files under `crates/cuda-device/src/generated/`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:332
msgid "generated files under `crates/dialect-nvvm/src/ops/generated/`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:333
msgid "generated intrinsic dispatch in `mir-importer`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:334
msgid "generated intrinsic conversion tables in `mir-lower`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:335
msgid "generated target/collector metadata;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:336
msgid "generated probe/reference outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/catalog-generated-intrinsics.md:338
msgid ""
"If regeneration overwrites a hand edit, the edit was made at the wrong "
"layer. The source of truth is the reviewed catalog input, ABI, evidence, or "
"generator logic that owns that output."
msgstr ""
